; Eleven lookups where ten are allowed.
;
; Every other part of this policy is defensible. The SPF record is not: a, mx
; and nine includes come to eleven DNS lookups, and a receiver stops counting
; at ten and returns permerror — which most treat as no SPF record at all. So
; this domain's carefully assembled sender list protects nothing.
;
; Edict counts eleven because it counts what it can see. It does not follow a
; single one of those includes, and each of them may spend lookups of its own,
; so eleven is the floor.
;
; Expected: a low grade, earned entirely by one line.

budget.example.         300 IN MX  10 mail.budget.example.

budget.example.         300 IN TXT "v=spf1 a mx include:_spf.crm.example include:_spf.invoices.example include:_spf.helpdesk.example include:_spf.newsletter.example include:_spf.payroll.example include:_spf.surveys.example include:_spf.events.example include:_spf.status.example include:_spf.legacy.example ~all"

_dmarc.budget.example.  300 IN TXT "v=DMARC1; p=reject; rua=mailto:dmarc@budget.example"

sel1._domainkey.budget.example. 300 IN TXT "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; "
